WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.906
Have you been able to get 

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.576
your COVID-19 jab yet?

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.044
Many countries are rolling out

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.179
the COVID-19 vaccines

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.049
so that the pandemic will be over 

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.585
and we can get back to normal.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.534
If you’ve never had COVID-19, 

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.568
your body doesn’t know 

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.037
how to fight it off.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.139
Vaccines help train 

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.306
your immune system

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.108
to recognize the virus 

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.010
and be ready to attack.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.745
But as we all have 

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.714
different immune systems, 

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.982
we respond differently

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.818
to the vaccine and the virus.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.653
Having side effects

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.687
has nothing to do 

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.624
with the effectiveness of the vaccine.  

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.826
So let's see what's going on 

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.327
once you get the jab.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.266
Congratulations!

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.468
You’ve just had your first dose

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.870
of the COVID-19 vaccine. 

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.938
For this episode,

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.774
we'll be focusing on messenger RNA,

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.710
or mRNA vaccines.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.412
Once it enters your body,

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.381
the mRNA vaccine

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.149
instructs your cells 

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.752
to create a spike protein.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.220
This simulates

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.190
part of the SARS-CoV-2 viral structure 

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.925
and tricks your body 

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.894
into believing that it's been infected.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.763
The spike proteins will then

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.132
head to the surface of your cell.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.534
Your immune cells will detect

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.670
these proteins that don't belong 

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.706
and begin making antibodies.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.141
If you happen to catch the virus

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.309
 in the future,

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.044
these antibodies will attach

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.679
 to the spike proteins on both 

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.647
your infected cells

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.583
and the coronavirus.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.717
This will mark them 

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.586
for immediate termination

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.821
by your immune cells.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.622
To be clear, 

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:06.059
the mRNA does not change your DNA 

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.994
in any way. 

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.596
Hear what I say?

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.931
Once the spike proteins are made, 

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.235
your body destroys the mRNA. 

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.377
Five minutes after your vaccine shot, 

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:27.714
you'll feel some soreness in your arm.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.481
To be safe,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.517
the Centers for Disease Control

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.751
recommends you stay

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.253
at the vaccination site 

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.688
for at least 15 minutes

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.991
in case of a severe reaction.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.958
While it's rare,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.060
you could have anaphylaxis,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.464
which is an immediate allergic response.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.566
It causes a series of symptoms

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:50.069
such as hives or swelling.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:50.803
Thankfully, 

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.438
trained healthcare personnel

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.439
will be available

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.375
at every vaccination site

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.809
to treat you immediately

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.912
with epinephrine.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.613
And according to the CDC,

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.681
you have a greater chance

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.516
of being struck by lighting,

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.552
around one in 500,000,

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.620
than having an allergic reaction.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.293
Four hours after your vaccine,

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:16.062
you could feel nothing at all.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.230
Lucky you.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.766
But you could also get a slight headache

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.467
or a low-grade fever

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.169
and feel tired.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.205
This is perfectly normal

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:27.407
and is a sign that your immune system

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.275
has kicked into action.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.580
At this point,

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.149
you may experience mild symptoms

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:39.552
as your body acclimatizes to the vaccine.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.522
You might feel tired and feverish.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.190
Be sure to get some rest

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.193
and take the day off work if you need to.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.062
After about 48 hours,

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.598
you should start to feel normal again.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:52.732
So let’s keep going.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:58.271
Okay, if you got the Pfizer

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.772
or Moderna vaccine,

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:00.340
you’d need to get

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.075
your second booster shot

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.978
three to four weeks after the first dose.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.045
Your immune system

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.514
would be stronger than the first time. 

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.916
But let’s see how it goes next. 

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.355
After your second dose,

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.757
you might feel crummy again. 

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.158
You could feel tired

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.093
feverish

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:22.061
and you might get the chills.  

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.063
These reactions are more common

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:26.799
after the second dose of the vaccine. 

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.836
But they’re mainly mild to moderate

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.771
and usually go away in a day or two.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:38.311
And two weeks after your second shot,

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.746
you’d be fully vaccinated

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:42.682
against the COVID-19 virus.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:46.052
So far, the Pfizer-BioNTech vaccine

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.388
has been 95% effective

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:51.057
at preventing COVID-19 illness. 

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.191
In either case,

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.493
the vaccine can prevent

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.094
hospitalization

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.095
and death

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.564
in people who have gotten sick.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.099
So getting a vaccine

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.534
is your safest path

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.902
to protect yourself,

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.470
your family 

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.807
and your community against this virus. 

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:10.610
It could also help reach herd immunity

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.545
by having vaccinated people

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.614
act as a barrier between

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.616
non-vaccinated people

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:20.119
and those who have been infected.  

